<task id="005" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Schema: `sprk_communication` privacy/internal-only/privilege/ACS-key columns + `communicationUserId` on user/contact</title>
    <phase>W0 — Phase 0 Verification + Foundation</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>4</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>001</dependencies>
    <blocks>042, 010</blocks>
    <tags>dataverse, schema</tags>
    <rigor-hint>STANDARD</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds columns to an EXISTING entity + a mapping column on user/contact — no BFF code, no Step 9.5 gates. STANDARD per §8. Modifies existing surface (column adds) — no §11 new-component justification required, but the columns must trace to FR-08 / ACS correlation.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W0-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-08</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add the `sprk_communication` columns that back privacy enforcement (FR-08) and ACS correlation, plus the ACS identity mapping on the user + contact entities. Schema only — the ENFORCEMENT (BFF query-filter) is task 042; the identity-minting LOGIC is task 010. This task just lands the fields so 042 and 010 have real columns to write/read.

    Add to **`sprk_communication`** (design §5, §8.2):
    - **privacy flag** — message-level privacy (composes with the thread-level privacy state on `sprk_communicationthread` from task 004).
    - **internal-only flag** — D-05 visibility attribute; external participants (R2/R3) never see these.
    - **privilege classification** — classification metadata DISTINCT from privacy; AI may *flag* but never *decide* (ADR-015). Composes with privacy.
    - **ACS `messageId`** — the ACS chat message id (the idempotency/echo-dedup key, design §4/§8.3).
    - **ACS `chatThreadId`** — the ACS thread correlation (also lives on the task-004 child table; confirm placement to avoid duplication — see notes).

    Add the ACS identity mapping:
    - **`communicationUserId`** on the **user** (`systemuser`) and **contact** entities — persists the ACS `communicationUserId` for sender resolution + token re-issue (design §8.2). Follow the 001 audit's confirmed target entities.

    Verify ALL option-set integers via Dataverse MCP before assignment (privacy/privilege choices if modeled as choices). Consume task 001's schema-audit report — add exactly what's MUST-ADD, do not recreate EXISTS columns.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema engineer. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill, option-set integer conventions, and the `sprk_communication` data model. You add exactly the columns FR-08 + ACS correlation require, verifying against the live schema first.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `sprk_communication` carries a message-level privacy flag, an internal-only flag, a privilege classification, and ACS `messageId` + `chatThreadId` correlation keys; the user + contact entities carry `communicationUserId`. All option-set integers verified via MCP; no existing column recreated. Task 042 (privacy enforcement) has real columns to filter on; task 010 (ACS identity) has a real mapping column to persist to.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §5 composes privacy from a SMALL number of `sprk_communication` + thread fields + BFF filters — "No new authorization engine." These columns are the data half; task 042 is the enforcement half. The ACS keys are the correlation half: `messageId` is the echo-dedup / idempotency key that lets outbound persist-on-send and inbound capture-on-event coexist (design §4); `communicationUserId` maps a Dataverse principal to its ACS identity so the BFF can mint tokens + resolve senders (design §8.2).

      §11 note: this task only ADDS COLUMNS to existing entities (no new component/entity), so the three-question §11 template does not apply (per CLAUDE.md §11 "Tasks that ONLY modify existing files ... do NOT require justification"). Each column still traces to a spec requirement: privacy/internal-only/privilege → FR-08; ACS `messageId` → FR-04/NFR-03; ACS `chatThreadId` → FR-05 correlation; `communicationUserId` → FR-03.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/spikes/001-schema-audit.md (task 001 output — the confirmed EXISTS/MUST-ADD delta; consume it)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/design.md (§5 privacy columns table, §8.2 identity mapping)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r1/spec.md (FR-08 + acceptance, FR-03)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design §5">Privilege classification is DISTINCT from privacy; AI may flag but never decide (ADR-015). Model them as separate fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §5 D-04">Message-level privacy composes with thread-level privacy (task 004). Point-forward switch logic is task 042 — this task only lands the fields.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §4 / §8.3">ACS `messageId` is the idempotency/echo-dedup key — ensure it is queryable/indexable for dedupe lookups (task 031 dedupes on it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="design §8.2">`communicationUserId` goes on BOTH `systemuser` and `contact` (per the 001 audit's confirmed targets). Persist the ACS identity for sender resolution + token re-issue.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Avoid duplicating the ACS `chatThreadId`: it is the thread↔channel child table's external-ref (task 004). If a per-message `chatThreadId` is also warranted for fast correlation, document WHY both exist (denormalized read key) — do not add it silently.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Verify ALL option-set integers via Dataverse MCP BEFORE assignment. Consume the 001 audit — add only MUST-ADD columns; do not recreate EXISTS.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">Author into the project solution per managed-solution conventions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Schema ONLY. No BFF enforcement (042), no identity-minting logic (010).</constraint>
  </constraints>

