  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`sprk_communication` carries: a message-level privacy flag, an internal-only flag, a privilege classification (distinct from privacy), an ACS `messageId`, and an ACS `chatThreadId` (with placement rationale documented).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`communicationUserId` exists on `systemuser` and `contact` (per the 001 audit targets).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ACS `messageId` column supports a dedupe/idempotency lookup (queryable/indexable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All option-set integers were verified via Dataverse MCP before assignment; no EXISTS column from the 001 audit was recreated.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No BFF enforcement logic and no identity-minting logic were added (schema only).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Blocks 042 (privacy/internal-only/privilege enforcement filters on these columns) and 010 (ACS identity persists `communicationUserId`). Depends on 001 (the audit delta).

    Watch the `chatThreadId` duplication: task 004 already puts the ACS thread id on the thread↔channel child table. Only add a per-message `chatThreadId` if there is a concrete read-path reason (denormalized correlation for dedupe/capture) — and document it. Do not create two sources of truth silently.

    These fields are inert without task 042's enforcement. Landing them here (W0-B, parallel with 004/006) keeps the security-sensitive enforcement task (042) unblocked on real schema.
  </notes>

